# Built frontend assets are shipped VERBATIM.
#
# frontend/dist/ is committed (see .gitignore) so every branch/tag zip has a
# working UI without npm. Those files are served with `Cache-Control: immutable`
# and their names are content-hashed, so the bytes a user downloads must be the
# bytes that were built -- a hash in the filename that does not match the body
# breaks long-lived caches. With core.autocrlf=true (as on Windows) git rewrites
# every line ending on checkout, which makes the downloaded copy differ from the
# built one. These are build outputs, never hand-edited, so no conversion.
frontend/dist/** -text

# Binaries that appear inside the build.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
